{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# Module 03 — Status\n**The documented method is executable AND wired.** C++/SPOT engine complete through Phase D, M01's property suite ingested, both vacuity channels closed, real HTTP service. Snapshot: 2026-07-30, `main-demo` @ `5c65046` (FINAL).","x":260,"y":-400,"width":700,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"py-real","type":"text","text":"**Track 1 — Pure-Python pipeline: INTACT (legacy Phase D)**\n~1,470 LOC core, 4 phases in `module_03_equiv/src/`.\n`run_pipeline` explicitly marked LEGACY (PR #77) — kept because its tests exercise components directly and it is the **only home of loop-bound checking** (open gap in the canonical path).","x":0,"y":-180,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cpp-now","type":"text","text":"**Track 2 — C++/SPOT engine: canonical, all phases A–D**\n`lifter.cpp` **1,423 LOC**; pybind11 `AdvancedLifter` + `cluster_implementations` + `check_compliance`.\n`process_wir_batch()` **declared the canonical Phase D** (PR #77) — the only path any real caller uses.","x":420,"y":-180,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ingestion","type":"text","text":"**M01 ingestion WIRED (PR #72)**\n`property_ingest.py` (205 LOC): loads `module_03_input.json`, tier-gates (node()-free P1 only — 17.6% of tier), de-dupes (34/412 in real corpus), normalizes to SPOT-ready **quoted** flat atoms (Option B). Ported, not imported — dual-track independence preserved.","x":840,"y":-180,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"vacuity","type":"text","text":"**Both vacuity channels CLOSED**\n1. Atom-matching gate (PR #67): unmatched atom → `INCONCLUSIVE`, never `VIOLATION`\n2. Alive-extension bridge (PR #70): `spot::from_ltlf` (De Giacomo–Vardi) + mutual-exclusion edge closure for non-looping automata — validated 100% agreement with M01's `evaluate_ltlf` oracle on all 35 decisive verdicts (58 checks, 29 specs)","x":0,"y":60,"width":400,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d2","type":"text","text":"**Definition-order defect FIXED via D2 (PR #73)**\nThe lifter used to see function *definitions* in definition order (wrong order in ~46% of corpus variants; gateways/tasks never in one graph). Now consumes Module 02's **call-order WIR** — business actions in execution order. `/check` documents that posting a definition-order WIR reproduces the old bug.","x":440,"y":60,"width":400,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"service","type":"text","text":"**Real HTTP service (PR #74)**\n`src/main.py` rewritten from the stale P1.1 print-and-exit demo into FastAPI: `POST /lift`, `POST /check`, `GET /health` (uvicorn :8000, docker CMD). M04's equiv page now works over HTTP like the other engines.","x":880,"y":60,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tests","type":"text","text":"**Tests: 142 functions / 6 files**\n37 pipeline · 34 C++ engine · 28 phase B · 21 phase C · 17 property ingest · 5 counterexample. C++-side `skipif` no `.so`.\nPre-existing gap unchanged: `compute_deterministic_hash` referenced by 2 phase-B tests, still unimplemented.","x":0,"y":330,"width":400,"height":190,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e2e","type":"text","text":"**E2E demonstrated + measured**\n`demo/e2e_demo.py` (PR #76): BPMN → M01 → M02 → M03 → verdict + readable counterexample on real FLOW-BENCH LLM implementations.\n`demo/eval_e2e/` (PR #77): abstention 0.462 · detection 0.357 · false-alarm 0.000 · cx quality 0.800 (small n, CIs).","x":440,"y":330,"width":400,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"open-gaps","type":"text","text":"**Open gaps (tracked, not hidden)**\n- Loop-bound safety checking has **no home** in the canonical path (`P2_Quality_Limits` excluded from conformance)\n- Non-terminating trace vs termination-requiring property: deferred design decision (looping automata skip the alive-extension bridge)\n- Checkable slice is the node()-free P1 subset (17.6% of tier) — widening needs event-lifecycle mapping + X-operator bridge\n- Phase A atoms depend on M02's call-order view being fed in","x":880,"y":330,"width":400,"height":250,"color":"1"}
	],
